<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines buys 150,000 T U.S. yellow corn.</title>
<headline>Philippines buys 150,000 T U.S. yellow corn.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-owned National Food Authority said on Tuesday it bought 150,000 tonnes U.S. yellow corn number two at an average price of $161.1 per tonne C&amp;F.  </p>
<p>NFA deputy administrator Eduardo Gomez told Reuters the agency awarded the contract to five commodity houses in a bidding this afternoon.</p>
<p>He said shipment of the commodity will be between November 9 to December 28. It will be done in six shipments, he said.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8936</p>
</text>
